---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Experiment 8.1: Energy of a Rubber Band">
    <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
        <div class="experiment-header">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-blue-700 mb-2">EXPERIMENT 8.1</h1>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center text-blue-700 mb-8">ENERGY OF A RUBBER BAND</h2>
        </div>

        <!-- Email Collection Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4">
                <h4 class="font-bold mb-2">Student Information:</h4>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                    <div>
                        <label for="studentName" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Name:</label>
                        <input type="text" id="studentName" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg" placeholder="Your Name">
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <label for="studentEmail" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Email:</label>
                        <input type="email" id="studentEmail" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg" placeholder="your.email@example.com">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-4">
                    <label for="teacherEmail" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Teacher's Email:</label>
                    <input type="email" id="teacherEmail" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg" value="chuck@c00lnerd.com" placeholder="teacher.email@example.com">
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Purpose Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">PURPOSE:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">To investigate the elastic potential energy and kinetic energy of a rubber band.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Materials Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">MATERIALS:</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-8 mb-4">
                <li>1—5 rubber bands (all must be the same thickness and length)</li>
                <li>A metric ruler</li>
                <li>Tape measure (one with metric units on it would be best)</li>
                <li>Masking tape</li>
                <li>Safety glasses or goggles</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Safety Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-yellow-700">SAFETY:</h3>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-8 mb-0">
                    <li class="text-red-600 font-bold">Make sure to never point the rubber band at anyone!</li>
                    <li>Always wear safety glasses or goggles during this experiment.</li>
                    <li>Conduct this experiment in an open area where the rubber band won't hit anything fragile.</li>
                    <li>Be careful when retrieving rubber bands to avoid tripping or falling.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Background Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">BACKGROUND:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">It would be best to do this experiment outside or in a long hallway because the rubber band will fly some distance. <span class="text-red-600 font-bold">Make sure to never point the rubber band at anyone!</span> You may also want a helper to help you spot and mark where the rubber band lands as sometimes it will bounce a bit.</p>
            
            <p class="mb-4">When you stretch a rubber band, you are storing elastic potential energy in it. This is a form of potential energy that is stored in elastic materials when they are deformed. The more you stretch the rubber band, the more potential energy is stored.</p>
            
            <p class="mb-4">When you release the rubber band, this potential energy is converted into kinetic energy - the energy of motion. The rubber band flies through the air because of this kinetic energy. The relationship between how much you stretch the rubber band (the potential energy you store) and how far it flies (the kinetic energy it receives) is what we'll be investigating in this experiment.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Questions Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">QUESTIONS:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">What is the relationship between the potential energy of a stretched rubber band and its kinetic energy once the rubber band is released? In other words, how will the potential and kinetic energy of a stretched rubber band affect the distance it travels?</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Hypothesis Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">HYPOTHESIS:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Write what you predict will happen to the rubber band (how far will it travel when released) when it is stretched to different lengths:</p>
            <textarea id="hypothesis" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="4" placeholder="Your hypothesis..."></textarea>
        </section>

        <!-- Procedure Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">PROCEDURE:</h3>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-8 mb-4 space-y-4">
                <li>
                    <p>Locate a long straight area to conduct your experiment. A driveway or sidewalk on a nice day is perfect. If that is not an option, choose a room that has a long, unobstructed area for you to shoot the rubber band. Select a starting spot and mark it with a strip of masking tape.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>With your feet behind the masking tape line, hook the rubber band over the front edge of the metric ruler and stretch it back to the 10 cm mark on the ruler. Keep the ruler level and let the rubber band go.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>If you have a helper, have them place a masking tape mark where the rubber band lands and return the rubber band to you. If you don't have a helper, you will need to mark the landing place and retrieve the rubber band. (You may also use other rubber bands as long as they are the same thickness and length.)</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Repeat steps 2—3 four more times for a total of 5 trials stretching the rubber band to 10 cm.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>With the tape measure, measure the distance in centimeters from the starting line to the landing point for each of the 5 trials. Record these distances in your data table. Pick up the masking tape marks after recording the distance.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Repeat steps 2—5, but stretch the rubber band on the metric ruler to 15 cm.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Repeat steps 2—5, but stretch the rubber band on the metric ruler to 20 cm.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Repeat steps 2—5, but stretch the rubber band on the metric ruler to 25 cm.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Average your distances for each stretch length by adding the distances together and then dividing by 5. Record the average in your data table.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>Make a graph of your results by putting the stretch length (in cm) on the x-axis and the average launch distance (in cm) on the y-axis. Plot your data points. What trend do you notice? Do your data points look like they form a straight line? If so, draw a line of best fit.</p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- Data Collection Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">DATA COLLECTION:</h3>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="min-w-full bg-white border rounded-lg">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th class="border p-2">Stretch Length (cm)</th>
                            <th class="border p-2">Trial 1 Distance (cm)</th>
                            <th class="border p-2">Trial 2 Distance (cm)</th>
                            <th class="border p-2">Trial 3 Distance (cm)</th>
                            <th class="border p-2">Trial 4 Distance (cm)</th>
                            <th class="border p-2">Trial 5 Distance (cm)</th>
                            <th class="border p-2">Average Distance (cm)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border p-2">10</td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="0" data-col="0"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="0" data-col="1"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="0" data-col="2"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="0" data-col="3"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="0" data-col="4"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" id="avg-0" class="w-full p-1 border rounded bg-gray-100" readonly></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border p-2">15</td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="1" data-col="0"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="1" data-col="1"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="1" data-col="2"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="1" data-col="3"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="1" data-col="4"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" id="avg-1" class="w-full p-1 border rounded bg-gray-100" readonly></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border p-2">20</td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="2" data-col="0"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="2" data-col="1"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="2" data-col="2"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="2" data-col="3"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="2" data-col="4"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" id="avg-2" class="w-full p-1 border rounded bg-gray-100" readonly></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border p-2">25</td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="3" data-col="0"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="3" data-col="1"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="3" data-col="2"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="3" data-col="3"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" class="w-full p-1 border rounded trial-distance" data-row="3" data-col="4"></td>
                            <td class="border p-2"><input type="number" id="avg-3" class="w-full p-1 border rounded bg-gray-100" readonly></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Graph Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">GRAPH:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Use the interactive graph below to plot your results, or create your own graph on paper.</p>
            <div class="border p-4 rounded-lg bg-white">
                <div class="w-full h-96 bg-gray-50 border rounded-lg">
                    <canvas id="graph-container"></canvas>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-4 text-center">
                    <p>Stretch Length (cm) vs. Average Launch Distance (cm)</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Conclusions Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">CONCLUSION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">What do your results show? What trend did you see on your graph? What does this tell you about the relationship between potential energy and kinetic energy? Write a paragraph explaining what you found and make connections to what you learned in the text.</p>
            <div class="mb-4">
                <textarea id="conclusion" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="6" placeholder="Write your conclusion here..."></textarea>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Analysis Questions Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">ANALYSIS QUESTIONS:</h3>
            <div class="space-y-4">
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">1. Based on your graph, what is the relationship between the stretch length and the distance the rubber band travels?</p>
                    <textarea id="question1" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">2. How does the potential energy of the rubber band change as you stretch it further?</p>
                    <textarea id="question2" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">3. What happens to the potential energy when you release the rubber band?</p>
                    <textarea id="question3" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">4. What factors might affect the accuracy of your experiment?</p>
                    <textarea id="question4" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold">5. How could you improve this experiment to get more accurate results?</p>
                    <textarea id="question5" class="w-full p-2 border rounded-lg" rows="2" placeholder="Your answer..."></textarea>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Extension Activities Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">EXTENSION ACTIVITIES:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Try these additional activities to further explore energy conversion:</p>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-8 mb-4">
                <li>Try the experiment with rubber bands of different thicknesses. How does the thickness affect the distance?</li>
                <li>Investigate how the mass of the rubber band affects the distance it travels by attaching small weights to the rubber band.</li>
                <li>Design an experiment to measure the efficiency of the energy conversion from potential to kinetic energy in the rubber band.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- Submit Section -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <div class="bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700 mb-4">SUBMIT YOUR RESULTS:</h3>
                <p class="mb-4">Click the button below to submit your experiment results to your teacher.</p>
                <button id="submitBtn" class="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded">
                    Submit Results
                </button>
                <p id="submissionMessage" class="mt-2 hidden"></p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>

<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
<script is:inline>
    // EmailJS loading and initialization with retry logic
    let emailjsReady = false;
    
    function loadEmailJS() {
        return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
            if (window.emailjs) {
                emailjsReady = true;
                resolve();
                return;
            }
            
            const script = document.createElement('script');
            script.src = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@emailjs/browser@4/dist/email.min.js';
            script.onload = function() {
                if (window.emailjs) {
                    try {
                        emailjs.init("ct_s19oZHppLy9BlW");
                        emailjsReady = true;
                        resolve();
                    } catch (error) {
                        console.error('EmailJS initialization failed:', error);
                        reject(error);
                    }
                } else {
                    reject(new Error('EmailJS failed to load'));
                }
            };
            script.onerror = function() {
                reject(new Error('Failed to load EmailJS script'));
            };
            document.head.appendChild(script);
        });
    }
    
    // Initialize EmailJS with retry logic
    function initializeEmailJS() {
        loadEmailJS().catch(error => {
            console.error('EmailJS loading failed:', error);
            // Retry after 2 seconds
            setTimeout(() => {
                loadEmailJS().catch(err => {
                    console.error('EmailJS retry failed:', err);
                });
            }, 2000);
        });
    }
    
    // Start loading EmailJS immediately
    initializeEmailJS();

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
        // Store student information in local storage
        const studentNameInput = document.getElementById('studentName');
        const studentEmailInput = document.getElementById('studentEmail');
        const teacherEmailInput = document.getElementById('teacherEmail');

        // Load stored values if they exist
        if (localStorage.getItem('studentName')) {
            studentNameInput.value = localStorage.getItem('studentName');
        }
        if (localStorage.getItem('studentEmail')) {
            studentEmailInput.value = localStorage.getItem('studentEmail');
        }
        if (localStorage.getItem('teacherEmail')) {
            teacherEmailInput.value = localStorage.getItem('teacherEmail');
        }

        // Save values when they change
        studentNameInput.addEventListener('change', function() {
            localStorage.setItem('studentName', this.value);
        });
        studentEmailInput.addEventListener('change', function() {
            localStorage.setItem('studentEmail', this.value);
        });
        teacherEmailInput.addEventListener('change', function() {
            localStorage.setItem('teacherEmail', this.value);
        });

        // Set up data table calculations
        const trialDistanceInputs = document.querySelectorAll('.trial-distance');
        trialDistanceInputs.forEach(input => {
            input.addEventListener('input', calculateAverages);
        });

        // Initial calculation on page load
        calculateAverages();
        
        function calculateAverages() {
            // For each row (stretch length)
            for (let row = 0; row < 4; row++) {
                let sum = 0;
                let count = 0;
                let values = [];
                
                // Get all trial values for this row
                for (let col = 0; col < 5; col++) {
                    const input = document.querySelector(`.trial-distance[data-row="${row}"][data-col="${col}"]`);
                    if (input && input.value && input.value.trim() !== '') {
                        const value = parseFloat(input.value);
                        if (!isNaN(value)) {
                            values.push(value);
                            sum += value;
                            count++;
                        }
                    }
                }
                
                // Update the average field
                const avgInput = document.getElementById(`avg-${row}`);
                if (count > 0) {
                    const average = sum / count;
                    avgInput.value = average.toFixed(2); // Increased to 2 decimal places for more significant figures
                    console.log(`Row ${row}: Values=${values.join(', ')}, Sum=${sum}, Count=${count}, Avg=${average}`);
                } else {
                    avgInput.value = '';
                }
            }
            
            // Only update the graph when averages change, and use a debounce to prevent too frequent updates
            clearTimeout(window.graphUpdateTimer);
            window.graphUpdateTimer = setTimeout(updateGraph, 300);
        }
        
        // Create chart only once when page loads
        let rubberBandChart = null;
        
        // Initialize chart once when page is loaded
        window.addEventListener('load', function() {
            const canvas = document.getElementById('graph-container');
            if (canvas) {
                const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
                
                rubberBandChart = new Chart(ctx, {
                    type: 'scatter',
                    data: {
                        datasets: [{
                            label: 'Rubber Band Data',
                            data: [],
                            backgroundColor: 'rgba(54, 162, 235, 0.6)',
                            borderColor: 'rgba(54, 162, 235, 1)',
                            borderWidth: 1,
                            pointRadius: 6
                        }]
                    },
                    options: {
                        responsive: true,
                        maintainAspectRatio: true,
                        animation: false,
                        scales: {
                            x: {
                                title: {
                                    display: true,
                                    text: 'Stretch Length (cm)'
                                },
                                min: 5,
                                max: 30
                            },
                            y: {
                                title: {
                                    display: true,
                                    text: 'Average Launch Distance (cm)'
                                },
                                min: 0
                            }
                        }
                    }
                });
            }
        });
        
        // Function to update the graph with current data
        function updateGraph() {
            if (!rubberBandChart) return; // Don't update if chart doesn't exist yet
            
            const stretchLengths = [10, 15, 20, 25];
            const dataPoints = [];
            
            for (let i = 0; i < stretchLengths.length; i++) {
                const avgInput = document.getElementById(`avg-${i}`);
                if (avgInput && avgInput.value) {
                    dataPoints.push({
                        x: stretchLengths[i],
                        y: parseFloat(avgInput.value)
                    });
                }
            }
            
            // Update existing chart data
            rubberBandChart.data.datasets[0].data = dataPoints;
            rubberBandChart.update('none'); // Update without animation
        }

        // Handle form submission
        const submitBtn = document.getElementById('submitBtn');
        const submissionMessage = document.getElementById('submissionMessage');

        submitBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
            // Disable button immediately to prevent multiple clicks
            submitBtn.disabled = true;
            submitBtn.textContent = 'Submitting...';
            
            // Validate required fields
            const studentName = studentNameInput.value.trim();
            const studentEmail = studentEmailInput.value.trim();
            const teacherEmail = teacherEmailInput.value.trim();
            const conclusion = document.getElementById('conclusion').value.trim();

            if (!studentName || !studentEmail || !teacherEmail) {
                showMessage('Please fill in all required student and teacher information.', 'error');
                return;
            }

            if (!conclusion) {
                showMessage('Please complete your conclusion before submitting.', 'error');
                return;
            }

            // Collect data from the experiment
            const hypothesis = document.getElementById('hypothesis').value.trim();
            
            // Get data table values
            let dataValues = {};
            for (let row = 0; row < 4; row++) {
                const stretchLength = [10, 15, 20, 25][row];
                for (let col = 0; col < 5; col++) {
                    const input = document.querySelector(`.trial-distance[data-row="${row}"][data-col="${col}"]`);
                    if (input) {
                        dataValues[`stretch_${stretchLength}_trial_${col+1}`] = input.value || 'Not recorded';
                    }
                }
                const avgInput = document.getElementById(`avg-${row}`);
                if (avgInput) {
                    dataValues[`stretch_${stretchLength}_avg`] = avgInput.value || 'Not calculated';
                }
            }
            
            const question1 = document.getElementById('question1').value.trim();
            const question2 = document.getElementById('question2').value.trim();
            const question3 = document.getElementById('question3').value.trim();
            const question4 = document.getElementById('question4').value.trim();
            const question5 = document.getElementById('question5').value.trim();

            // Prepare comprehensive experiment data matching working experiment format
            const questionsData = 
                '1. Based on your graph, what is the relationship between the stretch length and the distance the rubber band travels?\n' +
                (question1 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '2. How does the potential energy of the rubber band change as you stretch it further?\n' +
                (question2 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '3. What happens to the potential energy when you release the rubber band?\n' +
                (question3 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '4. What factors might affect the accuracy of your experiment?\n' +
                (question4 || 'Not answered') + '\n\n' +
                '5. How could you improve this experiment to get more accurate results?\n' +
                (question5 || 'Not answered');

            const stretchDataText = 
                `10cm Stretch: Trials: ${dataValues.stretch_10_trial_1}, ${dataValues.stretch_10_trial_2}, ${dataValues.stretch_10_trial_3}, ${dataValues.stretch_10_trial_4}, ${dataValues.stretch_10_trial_5}. Average: ${dataValues.stretch_10_avg}\n` +
                `15cm Stretch: Trials: ${dataValues.stretch_15_trial_1}, ${dataValues.stretch_15_trial_2}, ${dataValues.stretch_15_trial_3}, ${dataValues.stretch_15_trial_4}, ${dataValues.stretch_15_trial_5}. Average: ${dataValues.stretch_15_avg}\n` +
                `20cm Stretch: Trials: ${dataValues.stretch_20_trial_1}, ${dataValues.stretch_20_trial_2}, ${dataValues.stretch_20_trial_3}, ${dataValues.stretch_20_trial_4}, ${dataValues.stretch_20_trial_5}. Average: ${dataValues.stretch_20_avg}\n` +
                `25cm Stretch: Trials: ${dataValues.stretch_25_trial_1}, ${dataValues.stretch_25_trial_2}, ${dataValues.stretch_25_trial_3}, ${dataValues.stretch_25_trial_4}, ${dataValues.stretch_25_trial_5}. Average: ${dataValues.stretch_25_avg}`;

            const experimentData = 
                'EXPERIMENT 8.1: ENERGY OF A RUBBER BAND - DETAILED RESULTS\n\n' +
                'Student: ' + studentName + '\n' +
                'Email: ' + studentEmail + '\n\n' +
                'HYPOTHESIS:\n' + (hypothesis || 'Not provided') + '\n\n' +
                'STRETCH DATA:\n' + stretchDataText + '\n\n' +
                'ANALYSIS QUESTIONS:\n' + questionsData + '\n\n' +
                'CONCLUSION:\n' + conclusion + '\n\n' +
                'Experiment completed: ' + new Date().toLocaleString();

            // Disable button and show loading state
            submitBtn.disabled = true;
            submitBtn.textContent = 'Submitting...';

            // Check if EmailJS is ready before sending
            if (!emailjsReady) {
                showMessage('Email service is still loading. Please wait a moment and try again.', 'error');
                submitBtn.disabled = false;
                submitBtn.textContent = 'Submit Results';
                return;
            }

            // Send email using EmailJS with exact parameter structure from working experiment6_2
            emailjs.send('service_ot1jg6s', 'template_y556rhr', {
                student_name: studentName,
                student_email: studentEmail,
                experiment_title: 'Experiment 8.1: Energy of a Rubber Band',
                hypothesis: hypothesis || 'Not provided',
                missing_elements: questionsData,
                conclusion: experimentData,
                subject: `Experiment 8.1 - ${studentName}`
            })
                .then(function(response) {
                    console.log('SUCCESS!', response.status, response.text);
                    showMessage('Your experiment results have been submitted successfully!', 'success');
                    submitBtn.textContent = 'Submitted';
                })
                .catch(function(error) {
                    console.log('FAILED...', error);
                    showMessage('Failed to submit results. Please try again later.', 'error');
                    submitBtn.disabled = false;
                    submitBtn.textContent = 'Submit Results';
                });
        });

        function showMessage(message, type) {
            submissionMessage.textContent = message;
            submissionMessage.classList.remove('hidden', 'text-green-600', 'text-red-600');
            submissionMessage.classList.add(type === 'success' ? 'text-green-600' : 'text-red-600');
        }
    });
</script>
